  "caveats": [
    "All methods introduced after earlier source effects were observed, hence post-selection sensitivity, not external independent validation.",
    "The strict all-fix-inside-30km rule can wrongly exclude genuine temporary foraging excursions.",
    "Overlapping stationary-day source windows and shared synoptic weather remain correlated beyond calendar month weather blocks.",
    "The shorebird source temperature difference reverses sign under stricter GPS stationarity, but neither sign is causal or cross-taxon confirmation.",
    "Stork shortwave and goose wind-speed patterns are within their original cohorts only; flight altitude, turbulence, actual site-departure decisions, energy costs and fitness are unobserved.",
    "Vulture has too few clean case days with within-grid-year-month stayed source records; no new meteorology or effect fit was made for vulture.",
    "2016 versus 2018 stork studies have shared tag IDs, so cohort-level independence cannot be inferred solely from differing paper or Study IDs."
  ]
